\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Weak transfer and continued skill use at the same later depth. Copying skill-position states from a correct-skill run into an unrelated-skill run gives strong early recovery (left) and weak late recovery (middle). At that same later depth, the original run still needs skill access: retaining access preserves performance, while cutting it reduces accuracy (right). S and Q label skill and question tokens. Figure\nonbreakingspace \ref {fig:transferreading} gives the measured depth profiles.}}{1}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:teaser}{{1}{1}{Weak transfer and continued skill use at the same later depth. Copying skill-position states from a correct-skill run into an unrelated-skill run gives strong early recovery (left) and weak late recovery (middle). At that same later depth, the original run still needs skill access: retaining access preserves performance, while cutting it reduces accuracy (right). S and Q label skill and question tokens. Figure~\ref {fig:transferreading} gives the measured depth profiles}{figure.caption.5}{}}
