\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Timing of state repair, cache repair and the reading cut in the receiver. The prefix contains all prompt tokens except the last. (a) $S$ copies donor source states at block $L$'s output during prefix prefill. (b) $C$ copies source-position key/value (KV) entries at layers $0$ through $L$ after prefix prefill, before final-token recomputation. $SC$ combines these two writes, then recomputes the final prompt token and generates. (c) $SC+\mathrm  {cut}$ installs a reading mask before prefill, blocking reader-to-source attention from $L+1$ onward during prefill and decoding. Source-to-source attention remains unmasked. Reader states and caches evolve through computation rather than direct replacement. Figure\nonbreakingspace \ref {fig:mechanism}(b) separately tests cuts in the original correct-skill run.}}{3}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:design}{{2}{3}{Timing of state repair, cache repair and the reading cut in the receiver. The prefix contains all prompt tokens except the last. (a) $S$ copies donor source states at block $L$'s output during prefix prefill. (b) $C$ copies source-position key/value (KV) entries at layers $0$ through $L$ after prefix prefill, before final-token recomputation. $SC$ combines these two writes, then recomputes the final prompt token and generates. (c) $SC+\mathrm {cut}$ installs a reading mask before prefill, blocking reader-to-source attention from $L+1$ onward during prefill and decoding. Source-to-source attention remains unmasked. Reader states and caches evolve through computation rather than direct replacement. Figure~\ref {fig:mechanism}(b) separately tests cuts in the original correct-skill run}{figure.caption.10}{}}
