\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Repair and attention cuts across four models and two benchmarks. MC denotes MedCalc and TQA denotes TheoremQA. (a) Receiver accuracy at $L16$ for state replacement ($S$), cache replacement ($C$), joint repair ($SC$), and joint repair with a reading cut from $L17$ onward ($SC+\mathrm  {cut}$). (b) Correct answers lost in the original correct-skill run under cuts from $L8$, $L16$ or $L24$ onward during prefill and decoding. Skill reading blocks reader-to-source attention. Within-skill attention blocks source-to-source attention. Each row uses the same questions in both panels, with counts in Table\nonbreakingspace \ref {tab:mechanism-contrasts}. Layer numbers index each model's blocks.}}{7}{figure.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{4}{7}{Repair and attention cuts across four models and two benchmarks. MC denotes MedCalc and TQA denotes TheoremQA. (a) Receiver accuracy at $L16$ for state replacement ($S$), cache replacement ($C$), joint repair ($SC$), and joint repair with a reading cut from $L17$ onward ($SC+\mathrm {cut}$). (b) Correct answers lost in the original correct-skill run under cuts from $L8$, $L16$ or $L24$ onward during prefill and decoding. Skill reading blocks reader-to-source attention. Within-skill attention blocks source-to-source attention. Each row uses the same questions in both panels, with counts in Table~\ref {tab:mechanism-contrasts}. Layer numbers index each model's blocks}{figure.caption.29}{}}
