\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Complete-source controls across four models and two benchmarks. Entries are accuracy (\%). MC and TQA denote MedCalc and TheoremQA. Wrong and Neutral are the receiving contexts; Base is their unmodified accuracy. $C_{\mathrm  {all}}$ copies source KV at every layer; $SC$ additionally patches source hidden states at the stated layer. $B$ copies only other prefix KV, Full copies the complete prefix KV, and Replay copies all source KV then recomputes the later prompt. Full also gives donor accuracy. These pools differ from Table\nonbreakingspace \ref {tab:mechanism-contrasts}. Explicit all-layer rewriting after $SC$ leaves every generated token unchanged. Bold marks the highest accuracy among the three $SC$ depths in each row (ties included).}}{8}{table.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:state-completeness}{{3}{8}{Complete-source controls across four models and two benchmarks. Entries are accuracy (\%). MC and TQA denote MedCalc and TheoremQA. Wrong and Neutral are the receiving contexts; Base is their unmodified accuracy. $C_{\mathrm {all}}$ copies source KV at every layer; $SC$ additionally patches source hidden states at the stated layer. $B$ copies only other prefix KV, Full copies the complete prefix KV, and Replay copies all source KV then recomputes the later prompt. Full also gives donor accuracy. These pools differ from Table~\ref {tab:mechanism-contrasts}. Explicit all-layer rewriting after $SC$ leaves every generated token unchanged. Bold marks the highest accuracy among the three $SC$ depths in each row (ties included)}{table.caption.36}{}}
